@.str.119 = private unnamed_addr constant [2799 x i8] c"Creates an oriented bounding box with various algorithms.\0A\0AArgs:\0A    points (open3d.core.Tensor): A list of points with data type of float32 or \0A        float64 (N x 3 tensor, where N must be larger than 3).\0A    robust (bool): If set to true uses a more robust method which works in \0A        degenerate cases but introduces noise to the points coordinates.\0A    method (open3d.t.geometry.OrientedBoundingBox.Method): This is one of \0A        ``PCA``, ``MINIMAL_APPROX``, ``MINIMAL_JYLANKI``. \0A\0A        - ``PCA`` computes an oriented bounding box using the principal component\0A          analysis. The output is in most cases not a minimal oriented bounding box.\0A          This algorithm is the fastest.\0A        - ``MINIMAL_APPROX`` is a fast approximation algorithm. The algorithm \0A          makes use of the fact that at least one edge of the convex hull must be\0A          collinear with an edge of the minimum bounding box: for each triangle in\0A          the convex hull, calculate the minimal axis aligned box in the frame of\0A          that triangle. At the end, return the box with the smallest volume.\0A          This algorithm is a good choice if speed and accuracy is important.\0A        - ``MINIMAL_JYLANKI`` computes an oriented bounding box using a more \0A          accurate but slower algorithm. This algorithm is inspired by the article \0A          \22An Exact Algorithm for Finding Minimum Oriented Bounding Boxes\22 \0A          written by Jukka Jyl\C3\A4nki. The original implementation can be found at \0A          the following address:\0A          https://github.com/juj/MathGeoLib/blob/55053da5e3e55a83043af7324944407b174c3724/src/Geometry/OBB.cpp#L987\0A          This algorithm is the best choice if accuracy is most important.\0A\0AReturns:\0A    The oriented bounding box.\0A    \0A    For the ``PCA`` method the bounding box is oriented such that the axes are \0A    ordered with respect to the principal components.\0A\0A    For the ``MINIMAL_JYLANKI`` method the bounding box is oriented to be closest \0A    to the identity rotation matrix.\0A\0AExample:\0A    This example shows a comparison of all algorithms::\0A\0A        import open3d as o3d\0A\0A        bunny = o3d.data.BunnyMesh()\0A        mesh = o3d.t.io.read_triangle_mesh(bunny.path)\0A\0A        methods = [\0A            o3d.t.geometry.PCA,\0A            o3d.t.geometry.MINIMAL_APPROX,\0A            o3d.t.geometry.MINIMAL_JYLANKI,\0A        ]\0A\0A        obbs = []\0A        for method, color in zip(methods, [(1,0,0),(0,1,0),(0,0,1)]):\0A            obb = o3d.t.geometry.OrientedBoundingBox.create_from_points(\0A                mesh.vertex.positions, method=method)\0A            obb.set_color(color)\0A            obbs.append(obb)\0A            print(f\22Volume is {obb.volume()} with {method.name}\22)\0A            \0A        o3d.visualization.draw([obb.to_legacy() for obb in obbs] + [mesh])\0A\00", align 1
